{"task_id": "two_sum", "prompt": "Implement `two_sum(nums, target)` returning the indices [i, j] (i < j) of the two numbers that add up to target. Assume exactly one solution.", "checks": ["solution.two_sum([2, 7, 11, 15], 9) == [0, 1]", "solution.two_sum([3, 2, 4], 6) == [1, 2]", "solution.two_sum([3, 3], 6) == [0, 1]"], "max_turns": 4, "mock_attempts": ["def two_sum(nums, target):\n    # buggy: always returns the first two indices\n    return [0, 1]\n", "def two_sum(nums, target):\n    seen = {}\n    for i, n in enumerate(nums):\n        if target - n in seen:\n            return [seen[target - n], i]\n        seen[n] = i\n    return []\n"]}
{"task_id": "factorial", "prompt": "Implement `factorial(n)` for non-negative integers, with factorial(0) == 1.", "checks": ["solution.factorial(0) == 1", "solution.factorial(5) == 120", "solution.factorial(6) == 720"], "max_turns": 4, "mock_attempts": ["def factorial(n):\n    # buggy: base case is wrong, factorial(0) recurses forever\n    if n == 1:\n        return 1\n    return n * factorial(n - 1)\n", "def factorial(n):\n    if n <= 1:\n        return 1\n    return n * factorial(n - 1)\n"]}
